WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.666 --> 00:00:03.666
Let's install the new Google Cloud Client Libraries for .NET

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:06.666
Google Cloud libraries are published as NuGet packages to integrate

00:00:06.666 --> 00:00:09.666
with Google Cloud services such as BigQuery, Pub/Sub and

00:00:09.666 --> 00:00:09.800
Cloud Storage. First, let's install Google Cloud SDK for Windows.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.033
Before we can use these libraries

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:15.033
We need to install Google Cloud SDK for Windows

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:18.033
Setup authentication using gcloud auth login command

00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:21.666
Now, let's go to Visual Studio and create a console

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:24.666
application to talk to Cloud Storage as an example

00:00:30.666 --> 00:00:33.666
Once the project is created, right click on references and

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.633
manage NuGet packages. Make sure include pre-release

00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:36.333
is selected. 

00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:37.533
Search for 

00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.533
Google.Storage.V1

00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:41.533
for Cloud Storage and install

00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:47.533
NuGet pulls down the package along with its dependencies

00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.833
Now, you're ready to use it in your application to talk to Cloud Storage

00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:55.833
For more information, see the links in the description

